  "raw_label": "-1",
  "texts": {
    "preamble": "M/S Shubham Industries vs State Of U.P. And Others on 7 February, 2020 Author: Sudhir Agarwal Bench: Sudhir Agarwal High Court Of Judicature At Allahabad ?Court No. - 34 Case :- Application U/S 482 No. - 7635 of 2005 Applicant :- M/S Shubham Industries Opposite Party :- State of U.P. and Others Counsel for Applicant :- Syed Ali Murtaza",
    "facts": "2. This application under Section 482 Cr.P.C. has been filed praying for quashing of proceedings in Criminal Complaint Case No. 778 of 1998, under Sections 7(V), 16(I)(a)(II) of prevention of Food Adulteration Act read with Rule 32(e)(f) of Prevention of Food Adulteration Rules, pending in the Court of 1st Additional Chief Judicial Magistrate, Basti. 3. It is contended that no sanction has been obtained but it is a question of fact which objection, if taken by applicant, can be examined by Court below.",
    "arguments": "Recently in Md. Allauddin Khan Vs. The State of Bihar and others (2019) 6 SCC 107, Supreme Court observed as to what should be examined by High Court in an application under Section 482 Cr.P.C. and in paras 15, 16 and 17 said as under : ?15. 4. Very recently, Apex Court in Criminal Appeal No. 1817 of 2019 (M. Jayanthi Vs. K.R. Meenakshi and another) decided on 02.12.2019 has held: ?It is too late in the day to seek reference to any authority for the proposition that while invoking the power underSection 482 Cr.P.C for quashing a complaint or a charge, the Court should not embark upon an enquiry into the validity of the evidence available.",
    "petitioner_arguments": "",
    "respondent_arguments": "",
    "other_lawyer_arguments": "Recently in Md. Allauddin Khan Vs. The State of Bihar and others (2019) 6 SCC 107, Supreme Court observed as to what should be examined by High Court in an application under Section 482 Cr.P.C. and in paras 15, 16 and 17 said as under : ?15. 4. Very recently, Apex Court in Criminal Appeal No. 1817 of 2019 (M. Jayanthi Vs. K.R. Meenakshi and another) decided on 02.12.2019 has held: ?It is too late in the day to seek reference to any authority for the proposition that while invoking the power underSection 482 Cr.P.C for quashing a complaint or a charge, the Court should not embark upon an enquiry into the validity of the evidence available."
  },
